From: Phil Taylor <phil@m0vse.uk>
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: qcom: avoid NAND training writes on Cambium X7-35X

The SDK serial-training routine erases and programs a training page during
probe, before read-only fixed partitions are registered. Miami recovery
must preserve the complete OEM NAND, including its training partition.
Use the supported 50 MHz feedback-clock mode on this exact board instead.
Do not change other boards' training or the Miami NAND/ECC layout.

Signed-off-by: Phil Taylor <phil@m0vse.uk>
--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/qcom_nandc.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/qcom_nandc.c
@@ -3714,6 +3714,13 @@
 			reg) | FEEDBACK_CLK_EN),
 			NAND_QSPI_MSTR_CONFIG);
 
+	/* Recovery must not erase/program OEM training data during probe. */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("cambiumnetworks,x7-35x")) {
+		dev_info(nandc->dev,
+			 "Miami: preserve NAND training data, use 50MHz feedback clock\n");
+		return clk_set_rate(nandc->iomacro_clk, IO_MACRO_50_MHZ);
+	}
+
 	/* Read the training offset patched from u-boot */
 	if (of_property_read_u32(np, "qcom,training_offset",
 				&training_offset)) {
